Project Design Phase

1. Introduction

The Project Design Phase describes how the proposed system will be structured and developed based on the requirements identified in the previous phase.

2. Objectives

- Design the overall system architecture.
- Define the modules of the project.
- Plan the database structure.
- Design the user interface.
- Identify the technologies required for development.

3. System Architecture

System architecture explains the overall structure of the application and how its different components interact with each other.

4. Database Design

Database design defines how data will be stored, organized, and managed efficiently.

5. User Interface Design

The user interface design focuses on creating simple, user-friendly screens for users to interact with the application.

6. Module Design

The project is divided into separate modules to make development, testing, and maintenance easier.

7. Technology Selection

The required programming languages, frameworks, database systems, and development tools are selected based on project requirements.

8. Expected Outcome

A complete design plan that serves as a blueprint for the implementation phase.

9. Conclusion

The Project Design Phase provides a clear structure for developing an efficient, reliable, and user-friendly system.
